   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_20"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Is there a way to read in bed without keeping my wife awake, Moshi?",
   "est_sec": 4.44,
   "gap_before": 0.59,
   "block": "books.dlg9",
   "kind": "moshi_name",
   "name_pos": "end",
   "addressee": "Moshi",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "A small clip on reading light with a warm, dim bulb works well. Or an e-reader with a backlight you can turn way down.",
   "est_sec": 7.54,
   "gap_before": 0.78,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg9"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "She says even turning pages bugs her.",
   "est_sec": 2.27,
   "gap_before": 0.82,
   "block": "books.dlg9",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Then an e-reader is your friend, it's completely silent. Some people also switch to audiobooks with one earbud in.",
   "est_sec": 5.99,
   "gap_before": 0.96,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg9"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I'd fall asleep in two minutes with an audiobook.",
   "est_sec": 2.89,
   "gap_before": 0.8,
   "block": "books.dlg9",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Most apps have a sleep timer, so it stops after fifteen or thirty minutes and you won't lose your place too badly.",
   "est_sec": 6.92,
   "gap_before": 0.38,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg9"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Okay, I'll",
   "est_sec": 0.72,
   "gap_before": 0.49,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "books.dlg9"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "try the timer thing tonight and see who falls asleep first.",
   "est_sec": 3.51,
   "gap_before": 2.6,
   "block": "books.dlg9",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
